    <string name="informed_consent_header">Informed Consent</string>
    <string name="informed_consent_title">INFORMED CONSENT</string>
    <string name="informed_consent_p1">We are the research team “Mama, Aku Kecanduan HP” from SMAN 70 Jakarta. We are currently conducting research entitled “PELUKDIRI (Perangkat Lunak Untuk Kesejahteraan Digital Remaja Indonesia): Control Theory-Based Screen Time Management System for Digital Health”.</string>
    <string name="informed_consent_p2">This study aims to determine whether using the PELUKDIRI application with adaptive cognitive challenge interventions can help reduce screen time duration, especially on entertainment apps, without significantly increasing user stress levels. PELUKDIRI is designed as digital wellbeing software that provides brief cognitive challenges in the form of mental math and patterns when respondents open designated entertainment apps.</string>
    <string name="informed_consent_p3">The benefit of this research is providing respondents with experience using technology designed to increase awareness of screen time usage. Furthermore, the findings are expected to serve as a basis for developing more adaptive digital wellbeing software suited for teenagers\' needs.</string>
    <string name="informed_consent_p4">The research method used is quantitative experimental research with a repeated measures design. Data collection is conducted via the PELUKDIRI app and questionnaires. Respondents will use the app during the study period, and screen time and intervention activity data will be analyzed to observe screen time changes.</string>
    <string name="informed_consent_p5">This study is conducted online via each respondent\'s smartphone. Respondents will use PELUKDIRI during the specified study period. During the study, respondents are asked to use their smartphones normally without intentionally changing their device usage habits.</string>
    <string name="informed_consent_p6">When opening selected entertainment apps configured for intervention, PELUKDIRI will display a brief cognitive challenge before the app can be used. Intervention levels can be adjusted based on respondent performance in solving challenges within established difficulty thresholds.</string>
    <string name="informed_consent_p7">During the study, the app will collect necessary research data such as screen time duration, entertainment app usage duration, app launch counts, and intervention activity and performance. Respondents will also be asked to complete questionnaires providing feedback on their app experience.</string>
    <string name="informed_consent_p8">PELUKDIRI does not read personal messages, photos, videos, contacts, passwords, or personal conversations. Collected data is used strictly for research purposes.</string>
    <string name="informed_consent_p9">App usage may cause minor discomfort, such as feeling interrupted when interventions appear or brief inconvenience in pausing entertainment app usage. Respondents may also experience difficulty with mental math or pattern challenges. Interventions are designed as short challenges with predetermined difficulty bounds.</string>
    <string name="informed_consent_p10">Obtained data will be kept confidential and accessible only by researchers. Research data will be stored locally on researcher laptops. Respondent identities will be anonymized with codes during processing and omitted from research publications. Results will be presented in group data, tables, charts, or statistical analysis so individual identities remain unknown.</string>
    <string name="informed_consent_p11">Participation in this study is voluntary and follows research procedures and consent from respondents and parents or guardians. Respondents will receive compensation of IDR 50,000.00 as appreciation for their time and participation. Compensation is not coercion to participate.</string>
    <string name="informed_consent_p12">If you have any questions, app usage difficulties, or inquiries regarding this study, you may contact: josuaku091010@gmail.com (Joshua Leonardo Hilman Hutajulu) and daffa.satya.alif@gmail.com (Daffa Satya Alif Siregar).</string>
